  "generation_prompt": "Use case: reference-based isolated character rig layer. Generate exactly ONE transparent PNG asset: the INNER BACK LINING of the raised sleeve opening on the viewer-right side of this anime character. Reference 1 is the original fully clothed character; match its neutral light grey fabric, thin grey outline, flat restrained anime shading. Reference 2 is the approved raised-arm pose; focus only on the very narrow grey inside surface between the sleeve front hem and the arm. Output only this single complete inner-cuff backing, as a tall slim filled lens/oval of light grey fabric with a thin grey outer edge, viewed obliquely. It will sit behind both the white front sleeve and the arm, so provide a continuous full backing surface, no hole in its middle. Native intended visible shape about 34 px across and 155 px tall before slant, plus transparent padding. Its long axis leans about 12 degrees: TOP toward RIGHT, BOTTOM toward LEFT; the top tip is 30 px to the right of bottom at native scale. Use gentle curved sides and softly rounded narrow ends. Mostly pale neutral grey, a slightly darker right-edge strip; no black cavity or strong gradient. It is cloth, not skin. Do NOT draw white outer sleeve, torso, arm, hand, bracelets, character, diagrams, text, multiple pieces, rings or extra views. True alpha background; one isolated elongated lining layer only. Preserve clean thin line weight appropriate at the stated source scale. Original character is the style reference, not a request to redraw the character.\n",
